  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}\u20615\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u20615\\theta ]^{3}}=[\\operatorname{cos}\u20615\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u20615\\theta ]^{-3}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-3$ and $\\phi =5\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}\u20615\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u20615\\theta ]^{3}} & =[\\operatorname{cos}\u20615\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u20615\\theta ]^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5(-3)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5(-3)\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-15\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-15\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(15\\theta ).\n$$",
